    "description": "Objective\n\nA returning player should land back in the existing Sign-Up queue, not create a duplicate record.\n\nImplementation Requirements\n\n* When a new Study Link Click arrives for an existing Archived Sign-Up, and the click occurs AFTER a defined grace period has elapsed since archival, reactivate the Sign-Up instead of creating a new one\n\n* Grace period stored in a CUSTOM SETTING so admins can change it without editing automation. Set to 2 days for now\n\n* Archived Sign-Up is defined as Status = Archived AND not flagged for fraud\n\n* Fraud-flagged archived Sign-Ups are NEVER auto-reactivated\n\n* On reactivation: Status -> In Progress; clear Archive Reason and Other Reason (Archived)\n\n* Auto-reactivation applies ONLY when the click matches an existing Sign-Up on BOTH Player AND Deal. No match -> create a new Sign-Up as normal\n\nAcceptance Criteria\n\n* Click inside the grace period does not reactivate\n\n* Click outside the grace period reactivates and clears archive reasons\n\n* Fraud-flagged archived Sign-Ups are skipped\n\n* Non-matching clicks still create new Sign-Ups\n\nDependencies / ARCHITECTURE NOTE\n\nBUILD-04 (production Study Link Click resolution flow). This is a NEW BRANCH of that flow, not a standalone automation. Do NOT build a second record-triggered flow on Study Link Click — scope it into BUILD-04. See the pinned note on BUILD-04.\n\nEstimate: M · \\~10h (within BUILD-04)\n\nSource: Wagertech Additional User Stories, July 2026 — item 41.",
