        {
          "id": "10487",
          "body": "**SIMPLIFIED — Open Questions Q11 resolved. The grace period is gone.**\n\nDecision: \"If a click comes in for an archived sign up, it should be pushed back to **New** regardless of the elapsed time.\"\n\nSource: Lina via Emily Vandenberg, 2026-08-04 14:53 — \"spoke with Lina, there is no time window.\"\n\n**Changes to this card:**\n\n* **Strip the 2-day placeholder** and any custom setting / custom metadata holding a configurable window. No date maths at all.\n\n* Any click on an `Archived` Sign Up → Status = **New**, unconditionally. Not \"In Progress\".\n\n* Asymmetry to preserve: `Archived` reactivates, `Completed` does **not** (Q10 — log to Click History only, see BUILD-04).\n\n**⚠️ Undecided:** does reactivation clear `Archive_Reason__c` or retain it for history? Not covered by Q11 and it affects reporting. Recommend retaining the reason and stamping a reactivation timestamp, so the archive→reactivate cycle stays auditable. Needs a yes from Emily.",
          "created": "2026-08-10T13:08:42.564-0400",
          "updated": "2026-08-10T13:08:42.564-0400",
